{"agent":"dx-update","data":{"by":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_current` retrieves records by checking if `rid` is present in `st.bugs`, `st.lessons`, etc., or `st.schedules`, but `resolve` (lines 80-92) accepts a `kind:id` reference where the `kind` part is validated against `RF.ALL_KIND_NAMES`, `_data_kind(kind)`, or `\"rule\"`. If a user passes an arbitrary kind prefix not present in the specific hardcoded books or if `kind` and `rid` mismatch (e.g. `lesson:B1` where `B1` is a bug and not a lesson), `_current` raises a `KeyError` because `kind` is not a valid key for the lookup dictionary:\n```python\n        book = {\n            \"bug\": st.bugs,\n            \"lesson\": st.lessons,\n            \"research\": st.research,\n            \"decision\": st.decisions,\n            \"memory\": st.memories,\n            \"session\": st.sessions,\n        }[kind]\n```\nGiven input `ddflow update lesson:B1`, `resolve` returns `(\"lesson\", \"B1\", \"\")`, and `_current` crashes with a `KeyError` when attempting to subscript the dictionary with `\"lesson\"`.","digest":"43883a72e238d20f","family":"google","location":"ddflow/api/record_update.py:108","malformed":"","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/record_update.py:108"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"A missing id is distinguished from an ambiguous one by the substring `\"several\"` in the error text. `resolve` builds `no such record {ref!r}`, and the caller is supposed to get `None` so `items.update` can emit its own not-found. For any id whose rendered message contains that substring (`several`, `fix-several-bugs`, …) the condition fails and the function returns `O.refused(\"record.updated\", …)` instead of `None`. Given ref `several` and no such record, the caller never takes the not-found path.","digest":"336e33123c46e168","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/record_update.py:update_record","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/record_update.py:update_record"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Bare-id resolution never looks at rules, even though this module updates them when the ref is `rule:<id>`. `_candidates` scans bugs, lessons, research, decisions, memories, sessions, schedules, and defs only. A unique live rule `my-rule` with no other record of that id makes `resolve` return `no such record 'my-rule'`, and `update_record` returns `None` without calling `rule_update`. The same edit with ref `rule:my-rule` applies.","digest":"d446c17ffa2f0025","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/record_update.py:_candidates","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/record_update.py:_candidates"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"Fold aliases mutable event payloads into the live record. Lists are shallow-copied, but every other container is stored by identity: given `bug.updated` with `data.fields = {\"context\": {\"text\": \"x\"}}` (an own field allowed by the catalogue / `--set`), `setattr` binds that same dict onto the record. `rec.context[\"text\"] = \"y\"` then mutates `ev.data[\"fields\"][\"context\"]`, so a later replay or persisted event no longer matches what was recorded. The same leak hits a list-of-dicts field, because `list(value)` does not copy inner dicts.","digest":"176dbebf08b381e6","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/core/handlers/record_update.py:49","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/handlers/record_update.py:49"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"The new `set` parameter's `cli_help` is cut off mid-sentence: `` `ddflow help update` lists each kind's ``. `ddflow update --help` therefore prints an unfinished clause and never says what is listed (accepted fields / verbs), so the flag the change adds as the only path for own-fields and list folds does not document itself.","digest":"9eba8320f669bbca","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/queue.py:524","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/queue.py:524"},{"chunk":7,"detail":"`test_every_kind_has_a_catalogue_entry_with_every_op_decided` treats any truthy `kd.nearest` as covering every operation. A kind whose catalogue sets `nearest` to a non-empty string (or a dict that does not contain the op) and lists neither `title` nor `needs` in `attrs` or `declined` still passes: `op in kd.attrs or op in kd.declined or kd.nearest` is true because the third clause never checks that this `op` was decided. The suite can stay green while an op is neither accepted, declined, nor mapped to a nearest verb.","digest":"8cca0a71637b3e86","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_update_universal.py:126","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_update_universal.py:126"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"7/7 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":47645,"diff_sha":"c8ceb457882a3f47f34c5f950a597ecaecb4507e9aa5d45759069e58ee981845","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/DX-update-universal","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":166.0,"excluded_bytes":7580,"excluded_files":3,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr"],"family":"google","findings":6,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","output_digest":"9aeea648b992edf7","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-update-universal.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261111T085459Z-edd7d2ba.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"reviewed_head":"88407987384e01a2013fb572d059e582789c46fa","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 2c45bd3598122f0d18cd798c72b3ecc9909e7ff7","ddflow/api/items/_edit.py":"100644 1b5459d682d314bb7278784a1edf83e1392d4cd7","ddflow/api/record_update.py":"100644 32cf94f28accc4fdb86a37a773d14e9c5f87088a","ddflow/core/handlers/record_update.py":"100644 f71a081f163fe85872017a0fd6f635